Fixed the IP Fabric sync reporting IP Addresses and Cables as deleted while leaving them in the database. With Safe Delete Mode disabled each object is queued for removal under a grouping taken from its class name, and only four of those groupings were ever drained, so addresses and cables were dropped from the sync's own records and never removed. Every queued grouping is now drained, children before whatever they hang off, and a grouping the order does not name is removed last and reported rather than accumulating unread.
